text:
Another day of trying to keep up with everything happening in AI 😂

Raises, launches, open source projects, acquisitions…

Here’s what caught my eye:

1. Subvocal — $1.3M raised

@AarushYadav47 announced funding from YC and Afore Capital for glasses that turn silent mouthing into text. The pitch: communicate with your computer without typing or speaking out loud. Preorders are open.

2. Easol — $30M financing

@easol_ had a $30M financing package reported today: $20M equity and $10M debt. Its Teammates agents help event and experience businesses with sales, guest support and booking operations.

3. Talky — €1.5M pre-seed

Reported today, with the round closed in September. Talky learns how a company handles accounting, then helps process invoices, reconcile transactions and post entries into its existing finance systems.

4. Scenario — an entire 3D production toolkit for agents

@Scenario_gg announced 3D OS: an open-source collection of 80 skills covering modeling, animation, materials, lighting and game-ready exports. It works with coding agents and tools including Blender, Maya and Unreal.

5. Customuse — clean logos and text on 3D models

@customuse introduced Decals. Place your own logo or text on a model, then bake it into the texture or turn it into actual 3D geometry.

6. Runway — Agent can open files and run code

@runwayml expanded Agent’s capabilities for making brand launch kits, product shots, ad variations and motion graphics from references.

7. Glif — an AI modeling agency

@heyglif launched a cast of AI characters for images, films and campaigns. Choose someone, bring your product or brief, and create content around that character.

8. TBC — Mischief 1

@AlexKsendzovsky introduced an image-to-video model built on Wan 2.2, starting at half a cent per generated second. Its optimizations come from research with living neurons, translated into software running on standard AI hardware.

9. Dydema — programmable brain-computer interfaces

@dydema announced its approach to connecting trained thought patterns to computer actions, games or agents through a noninvasive interface. No surgery required.

10. Aura — open-source game playtesting

@Aura_Assistant open-sourced Autopilot, an agent that plays games and looks for bugs across Unity, Godot and Unreal. It can connect to Claude Code and Codex through MCP.

11. Unsloth — new local DeepSeek files

@UnslothAI released updated DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 GGUFs using Dynamic V3.1 quantization. These are new files for running the existing model locally, with updated benchmark results and setup instructions.

12. SAM3 — offline GPU support

@wkentaro_ added NVIDIA CUDA and Apple CoreML support to his SAM3 ONNX implementation. Identify and mask objects using text, boxes or clicks, with offline runs after downloading the model.

13. humans& — Ampersand Tutor

@humansand released &Tutor through its API. It trained the tutor through interactions with Persimmon, its model of human learners—an interesting approach for people building educational tools.

14. Voice Arena — Turing TTS

@voicearena_ai introduced an evaluation where listeners hear a human and an AI reading the same sentence, then identify the human. A different way to measure progress in synthetic speech.

15. OpenArt — IP Safety Check

@openart_ai launched a tool that scans images and videos for potential copyright and IP matches. It supports batches of up to 32 files with individual reports.

16. bricky — a LEGO compiler for agents

@maxencefaldor shared bricky. Your agent writes a Python build script; bricky places the pieces, flags construction mistakes and renders the result. It can also export a parts list.

17. diffmap — reviewing what your coding agent changed

@tanishqk introduced a document format and viewer for planning and reviewing agent code, using diagrams and linked code to explain design changes.

18. Factory — acquired Typedef

@FactoryAI acquired @typedef_ai, which builds a context layer for enterprise data. The goal is to give Droids better information for migrations, pipeline debugging and refactoring.

19. Claude — Ultra and limit changes

@claudeai renamed Max 5x to Max and Max 20x to Ultra. Prices stay at $100/$200. Five-hour limits are being removed for verified Ultra accounts, starting with most existing subscribers. Weekly limits remain.

20. Google — a response from orbit

@sundarpichai shared that Project Suncatcher’s prototype satellite ran a prompt on its onboard TPU and returned a complete response to Earth.

It wrote a haiku.

We’re sending prompts to space now.
